---

When something here stops being true, correct it in the same commit that made
it false. A stale line reads as authority: on 2026-08-17 one claimed a tool
offered a commit around every phase when it had been disabled by config the
whole time, and three sessions read the claim as fact before anyone ran it.

Keep the whole file under about 150 lines including the global rules it sits on
top of. Adherence falls off past that, so a rule added after the limit is not a
rule gained — it is one of the existing rules quietly lost.
